---
const title = "Ode to OpenCode | openlap";
const description = "A short ode to OpenCode from the openlap project.";
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <title>{title}</title>
    <meta name="description" content={description} />
    <meta property="og:title" content={title} />
    <meta property="og:description" content={description} />
    <meta property="og:type" content="website" />
    <meta property="og:url" content="https://openlap.dev/ode" />
    <style>
      :root {
        --bg: #fff6eb;
        --text: #3f2200;
        --muted: #8a6438;
        --accent: #784200;
        --accent-glow: rgba(120, 66, 0, 0.2);
        --blue-glow: rgba(162, 97, 31, 0.16);
        --border: rgba(120, 66, 0, 0.22);
        --panel: rgba(255, 249, 240, 0.94);
      }

      * { box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0; }

      body {
        min-height: 100vh;
        color: var(--text);
        background:
          radial-gradient(circle at 0% 0%, rgba(120, 66, 0, 0.08), transparent 30%),
          radial-gradient(circle at 100% 0%, rgba(120, 66, 0, 0.06), transparent 34%),
          var(--bg);
        font-family: Inter, -apple-system, Segoe UI, sans-serif;
        -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
        padding: 2.5rem 1.2rem;
      }

      .orb {
        position: fixed;
        border-radius: 50%;
        filter: blur(100px);
        z-index: 0;
        pointer-events: none;
      }

      .orb.green {
        width: 420px;
        height: 420px;
        top: -130px;
        left: 0;
        background: var(--accent-glow);
      }

      .orb.blue {
        width: 380px;
        height: 380px;
        top: -120px;
        right: 0;
        background: var(--blue-glow);
      }

      main {
        position: relative;
        z-index: 1;
        width: min(760px, 96vw);
        margin: 0 auto;
      }

      .back {
        display: inline-block;
        color: var(--accent);
        text-decoration: none;
        margin-bottom: 1rem;
        font-size: 0.92rem;
      }

      .back:hover { text-decoration: underline; }

      .card {
        border: 1px solid var(--border);
        border-radius: 0.9rem;
        background: var(--panel);
        padding: 1.4rem;
      }

      h1 {
        font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 4vw, 2.4rem);
        letter-spacing: -0.03em;
        margin-bottom: 0.3rem;
      }

      .sub {
        color: var(--muted);
        margin-bottom: 1.2rem;
        font-size: 0.95rem;
      }

      pre {
        white-space: pre-line;
        line-height: 1.78;
        color: #5f3a15;
        font-size: 1rem;
      }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <div class="orb green"></div>
    <div class="orb blue"></div>
    <main>
      <a class="back" href="/">Back to openlap</a>
      <article class="card" aria-label="Ode to OpenCode">
        <h1>Ode to OpenCode</h1>
        <p class="sub">The long-form version, preserved.</p>
        <pre>In terminals where old workflows queue,
OpenCode lands and cuts right through.
No tab parade, no modal maze,
just clean command-line lightning days.

Claude Code is solid, hats off there,
but this one feels like open air:
open source bones, repo in sight,
you can read the engine while it writes.

Anomaly ships with a grin and pace,
Dax drops spice, Adam keeps grace,
ship notes, jokes, and a "one more fix" spree,
then somehow still merge before three.

This is the future of how we build:
tools composable, context distilled,
humans steering, agents in stride,
and the terminal still where ideas ride.</pre>
      </article>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
